<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.5//EN"
"http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.5/docbookx.dtd">

<article>
  <articleinfo>
    <title>Graphics Build System</title>
    <subtitle>A Modular Build System for Graphics Projects</subtitle>
  </articleinfo>

  <section id="overview">
    <title>Project Overview</title>
    <para>
      This build system is designed to support complex graphics applications with a focus on:
    </para>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem><para>Cross-language integration (Python/Cython/C)</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Color space management and palette generation</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Robust error handling and logging</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Modular system architecture</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Future ImGui integration capabilities</para></listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </section>

  <section id="architecture">
    <title>System Architecture</title>
    <programlisting>
build-scripts/
├── lib/                 # Core utilities
│   ├── colors.sh       # Color and logging functions
│   ├── system.sh       # System detection and requirements
│   ├── python.sh       # Python-specific functions
│   └── packages.sh     # Package management functions
├── modules/            # Modular build components
│   ├── base.sh         # Base system setup
│   ├── python.sh       # Python environment setup
│   └── scientific.sh   # Scientific packages setup
├── templates/          # Project templates
├── config/            # Configuration files
└── build.sh           # Main build script
    </programlisting>
  </section>

  <section id="features">
    <title>Features</title>

    <section id="color-management">
      <title>Color Management System</title>
      <itemizedlist>
        <listitem><para>HSL-based color space transformations</para></listitem>
        <listitem>
          <para>Comprehensive palette generation:</para>
          <itemizedlist>
            <listitem><para>Monochromatic schemes</para></listitem>
            <listitem><para>Complementary colors</para></listitem>
            <listitem><para>Triadic color schemes</para></listitem>
          </itemizedlist>
        </listitem>
        <listitem><para>Pre-defined palettes (Ocean, Forest, Sunset, Berry, Mono Blue)</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Terminal color support</para></listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
    </section>

    <section id="build-capabilities">
      <title>Build System Capabilities</title>
      <itemizedlist>
        <listitem><para>Automated dependency detection and installation</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Virtual environment management</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Comprehensive logging with color-coded output</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Error tracking and reporting</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Support for scientific computing packages</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Cross-platform compatibility focus</para></listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
    </section>

    <section id="dev-environment">
      <title>Development Environment</title>
      <itemizedlist>
        <listitem><para>Python 3.8+ support</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Scientific computing setup (NumPy, SciPy, Pandas)</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Build tool integration (PDM, Meson, scikit-build)</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Testing framework setup</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Git integration with predefined .gitignore</para></listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section id="getting-started">
    <title>Getting Started</title>

    <section id="prerequisites">
      <title>Prerequisites</title>
      <itemizedlist>
        <listitem><para>Python 3.8 or higher</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>System build tools (documented in build_config.sh)</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Git for version control</para></listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
    </section>

    <section id="basic-setup">
      <title>Basic Setup</title>
      <programlisting>
# Clone the repository
git clone [repository-url]

# Run the build script
./build.sh

# Activate the virtual environment
source .venv/bin/activate
      </programlisting>
    </section>

    <section id="color-usage">
      <title>Color System Usage</title>
      <programlisting>
# Example: Generate a complementary color palette
source lib/colors.sh
source lib/palettes.sh
generate_complementary_palette 180 0.5 0.5
      </programlisting>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section id="development">
    <title>Development Workflow</title>

    <section id="building">
      <title>Building Projects</title>
      <orderedlist>
        <listitem><para>Configure project settings in <filename>config/defaults.sh</filename></para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Run the build script with desired modules</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Use the color management system for UI/UX development</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Implement tests following Red-Green Testing strategy</para></listitem>
      </orderedlist>
    </section>

    <section id="testing">
      <title>Testing</title>
      <para>
        The system supports a test-driven development approach:
      </para>
      <orderedlist>
        <listitem><para>Write tests in the <filename>tests/</filename> directory</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Run tests using PDM: <command>pdm run pytest</command></para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Implement features to pass tests</para></listitem>
        <listitem><para>Refactor while maintaining test coverage</para></listitem>
      </orderedlist>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section id="future">
    <title>Future Development</title>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem><para>ImGui integration for immediate mode GUI</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Vulkan/OpenGL graphics pipeline integration</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Extended color space support (RGB, CMYK, etc.)</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Additional palette generation algorithms</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>CI/CD pipeline integration</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Cross-platform testing enhancements</para></listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </section>

  <section id="contributing">
    <title>Contributing</title>
    <orderedlist>
      <listitem><para>Fork the repository</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Create a feature branch</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Implement changes with tests</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Submit a pull request</para></listitem>
    </orderedlist>
  </section>

  <section id="license">
    <title>License</title>
    <para>[License Type] - See LICENSE file for details</para>
  </section>

  <section id="acknowledgments">
    <title>Acknowledgments</title>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem><para>Color space conversion algorithms based on standard HSL/RGB transformations</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para>Build system architecture inspired by modern Python/C hybrid projects</para></listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </section>
</article>
